 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "BIGVILLE R7 (block 255000) -- housing TENURE (own/mortgage/rent), periodic payments, foreclosure/eviction -> HOMELESSNESS, tenure-driven EQUITY divergence, and the RENTIER lever. bf_mortgage_pay/miss are DISJOINT on the coin>=payment guard (an income collapse -> misses); bf_foreclose (missed>= term) transfers the LAND+building (owns_house edge) to the bank -- the ultimate collateral -- and sets homeless=1. bf_rent_pay/miss/evict mirror it for tenancy (the landlord keeps the house). bf_homeless_affect books the 204000/239000 distress (arousal up / valence down + social_concern), exactly like R4 be_default_affect. Equity DIVERGES by tenure: bf_owner_equity (=house.value), bf_mortgagor_equity (=max(0,value-balance), rises as balance falls) -- a RENTER matches NO equity rule so his equity stays FLAT at 0. bf_appreciate raises a house's value (owner/landlord equity rises; a renter owns none). bf_rent_raise is John-as-slumlord: raising rent moves the tenant's affect + backing (economic coercive control, 239/247). Every decision a RULE; composes existing Terms; zero new Rust.",
